><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Preoperative PaO<sub>2</sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.67</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.33-0.85</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0245</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Duration of cardiopulmonary bypass</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.15</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.55-6.21</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0171</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Intra-operative phrenic nerve injury</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.59</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.52-9.24</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0046</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Postoperative acute kidney injury</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.21</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.91-6.67</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0072</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>The <italic>Hosmer-Lemeshow</italic> goodness of fit coefficient of this model was 0.90. PPC, postoperative pulmonary complications; OR: odds ratio; CI: confidence interval; PaO<sub>2</sub>: arterial oxygenation.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>